### Z2 — println shapes that skip `c_guard_scan_idents`

Stmt `println` is **not** routed through `c_secret_emit_guard`:

```
c_emit_ident_stmt: id == "println" → c_emit_println
c_emit_println: per-arg token IDENT + c_secret_refuse_println_ident
                (no c_guard_scan_idents)
```

`eprintln` / `print_err` / `log` / `fprintf` / `syslog` **do** hit the
walker (free-call lower).

| # | Shape | Uses walker? | Live refuse? |
|---|-------|--------------|--------------|
| stmt `println(SECRET)` | **no** | **yes** — token walk + `check_secret_println_sinks` |
| stmt `println(n, SECRET)` | **no** | **yes** |
| stmt `println("esc", SECRET)` | **no** | **yes** (S71-10) |
| `eprintln(SECRET)` | **yes** | **yes** |
| empty `println()` | n/a (no ident) | emit-c rc=0 (no leak); check type `expects at least 1 argument` |

**Not fail-open:** skip of the C-text walker is covered by the token
IDENT rail (emit stmt + check/LLVM front-door). SPRINT **2.9**
(“println walker → full `c_secret_emit_guard`”) stays **MED residual**
(unify rails), not a 7.1 FN.

### Z3 — escape / string skip must not hide unquoted SECRET

These go through **`eprintln`** so the **walker** sees lowered C
`oo_str_lit("…"), api_key`.

| # | Source shape (after SECRET tag) | emit-c | check | llvm | HIDE? |
|---|----------------------------------|--------|-------|------|-------|
| 5 | `eprintln("foo\\", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| 6 | `eprintln("foo\"bar", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| 7 | `eprintln("\\", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| 8 | `eprintln("/* api_key */", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | — | **no** |
| 9 | `eprintln("//", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | — | **no** |
| 16 | `eprintln("foo\\\"x", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | — | **no** |
| 18 | `eprintln("\"", api_key)` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| 4 | `println("api_key")` string-only | ALLOW | ALLOW | ALLOW | n/a (**no FP**) |
| 11 | `eprintln("api_key")` string-only | ALLOW | ALLOW | — | n/a (**no FP**) |

Why hide is hard on product emit: `c_escape_str_text` always emits
well-formed C (`\\`, `\"`, `\\n`, `\\t`, 2-char controls). The walker’s
`\` + next-char skip then matches C string rules:

- even run of `\\` before `"` → `"` is closer → following ident is scanned
- odd run (`\"`) → quote is content → next `"` closes

**HIDE count: 0** on live well-formed emit text.

